  "limits": [
    "Only eight of the 57 visible captured SparseArrayBase records are reconciled in this transaction; 103 captured records include non-candidates. No full class or toolkit parity claim.",
    "Generic BasicIterator callable bodies were inspected and existing contracts replayed, but its exact overload/alias reconciliation remains separate; no arbitrary Rust bool specialization is selected.",
    "The unsafe erased API still requires valid stride/item alignment, callback object lifetimes, exclusive mutation and non-unwinding destruction. Over-aligned typed storage remains handled by its existing indirection adapter.",
    "Rust self-exchange uses explicit exchange_self; no aliasing pair of mutable references is constructed.",
    "Injected allocation resources and reset leases are Rust extensions; native protected constructor uses the common OCCT allocation functions. Allocation failure/panic and impossible Rust layouts are not credited as native exception equivalence.",
    "Native object allocation macros, callback type aliases, C++ iterator aliases, ABI/noexcept/configuration closure and destructor language semantics are not completed by these bindings."
  ],
